3518bc78_5bfbb56c",9,-10,1,"`TooManyKeys` currently doesn't exercise the `pthread_setspecific()` allocation / reentrancy path for two reasons: 1. `EnsureCreateKey()` is called here on line 211 *before* the `pthread_key_create`…"],["54b1cb3c_4a7acc6b",8,-10,1,"All callers ignore this return value. Should we return `void` here?"],["ada0e477_e3c950a9",8,-10,1,"`#include <pthread.h>` rather than `<unistd.h>` for `pthread_key_t`, `pthread_getspecific`, and `pthread_setspecific`."],["b35dbfaf_92c82299",8,-10,1,"Since `maybe_key_created_` is only ever modified while holding `creation_lock_`, would a single `std::atomic<bool> key_created_{false};` (checked with `load(std::memory_order_acquire)` on the fast…"],["ba75701f_dd4000ff",2,-10,1,"Nit: wording is a bit hard to follow here — did you mean: \"To support MiracleObject-quarantine, we need to guard against sanitizer hooks re-entering sanitizer hooks.\"?"],["d37ab9ed_0a0727b4",8,-10,1,"Consider moving the state check + initialization + transition to `kInsideShim` into a `PA_ALWAYS_INLINE static bool ReentrancyState::TryEnter()` method (or an `explicit operator bool()` on `Scope` /…"],["ed4e915e_407e26bd",8,-10,1,"Do we care that we're calling `GetState()` three times in DCHECK builds?"],["54e221d9_e24f03aa",8,-7,1,"please use `//`-style comments for consistency; see https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Comment_Style."],["5e8200b8_9a592753",8,-7,1,"also `key_created_.store(false, std::memory_order_release);`?"],["79ec30c9_7536bf43",8,-7,1,"omit trailing `*/`"],["ab6dc33b_0551bed6",8,-7,1,"`thread_ref` only exists in the `#if` block above. should this be: ``` Initialize(thread_ref); #else // PA_BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || PA_BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) Initialize(); #endif //…"],["ba68ea95_5e88e4f3",8,-7,1,"Is there a guarantee that this is always called during single-threaded setup before hooks are installed? If so, we don't need to check `key_created_` twice (and we don't need to include…"],["df1a70eb_319c24dd",8,-7,1,"